# deploy/research.Dockerfile's own ignore file. Docker looks for
# <dockerfile-path>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile and, when present,
# uses it INSTEAD of the repository's own .dockerignore for that build --
# so this file, not the top-level one (which excludes *.md wholesale, among
# other engine-only concerns), is what actually governs what reaches
# ohcamel-research's image.
#
# research.Dockerfile copies exactly four repo-relative trees: research/,
# interface/, fixtures/macro/ and fixtures/history/. Everything below either
# trims what those COPYs pull in, or drops trees none of them ever touch (kept
# out mainly to keep the build context this Dockerfile sends to the daemon
# small; no COPY here could reach them regardless).

# Never baked into any image: an image layer is permanent, and live mode's
# secrets reach the container through an env_file mount at runtime, never a
# COPY (see docker-compose.yml's ohcamel-research entry).
.env
.env.*
*.env

# Local, regenerated, or otherwise dev-only trees under research/ itself.
research/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Uncommitted battery run artifacts. research/experiments/ is otherwise
# copied whole, so its manifest.*.json files and each experiment's
# config.yaml -- both required for the staleness check below to run at all --
# reach the image with no pattern of their own.
research/experiments/*/results/

# Every markdown file, dropped by default (mirrors the top-level
# .dockerignore's own *.md/!README.md pair for the engine image) -- except
# the one research/ itself needs: research/pyproject.toml's `readme =
# "README.md"` makes hatchling refuse to build/install the project without
# it present (`uv sync --locked` in research.Dockerfile). Nothing else
# under research/experiments/ (hypothesis.md, report.md) or interface/ is
# read by the service or by is_stale -- see manifest.py: "no image needs
# report.md to show a strategy's evidence".
*.md
!research/README.md

# The manifests themselves are *.json, never touched by the *.md pattern
# above -- named here anyway, so this file says outright, not by omission,
# that research/experiments/*/manifest.*.json must reach the image.
!research/experiments/*/manifest.*.json

# Everything outside the four trees research.Dockerfile actually copies.
desk/
lib/
web/
bin/
test/
bench/
docs/
deploy/
.git/
.github/
.superpowers/
_build/
_opam/
_coverage/
book.sexp
book.example.sexp
desk.db*
Untitled
notes.txt
claudecodehandoff.md
*.pdf
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
